   "text": "I read the drawing as a resin-bound peptide, written here from the N-terminus to the resin. The sequence is H\u2011Arg(Pbf)\u2011Ser(tBu)\u2011Leu\u2011Pro\u2011Oic\u2011Ile\u2011Cys(Trt)\u2011Ile, linked as an ester to the resin bead through the C-terminal Ile.\n\n- **Arg:** the side chain is a propyl chain ending in a guanidine, with the Pbf (pentamethyl-dihydrobenzofuran-sulfonyl) group on the guanidine nitrogen.\n- **Ser:** the hydroxyl is protected as a tert-butyl ether.\n- **Leu and Pro:** both are unmodified.\n- **Oic:** this is the bicyclic octahydroindole-2-carboxylic acid. Both ring-fusion hydrogens are hashed, so the ring fusion is cis. I took the natural (2S,3aS,7aS) configuration.\n- **Ile (twice) and Cys:** the Cys sulfur carries a trityl group, and the C-terminal Ile is the resin ester.\n- **Resin:** the bead is written as a dummy atom `*` on the ester oxygen.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I assigned the L-configuration to all standard residues, which matches the wedges and hashes as I read them. For Oic I derived the CIP descriptors for the SMILES atom order I used.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)NS(=O)(=O)c1c(C)c(C)c2OC(C)(C)Cc2c1C)C(=O)N[C@@H](COC(C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1C(=O)N1[C@H]2CCCC[C@H]2C[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N[C@@H](CSC(c1ccccc1)(c1ccccc1)c1ccccc1)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)O*"
